 "doc": "FRAZZLED and blind, backing off: the near hand gropes low and sweeps for obstacles, the far hand shields his eyes, head ducked, short quick shuffling steps (12 f, 48 px each, 96 px per loop = 240 px/s), slippers barely lifting. Arm and head channels are set on every key so the half-cycle mirror (which swaps l/r) cannot swap which hand is groping; the torso is left to the poses because it is the root part and moving it slides the planted foot. The bouffant flip is the residue's.",
